        "ImageDescription": {
          "value": "<p>The Right Guard\nThe pair of noble soldiers guarding the tomb's entrance wear kausias (Macedonian flat hat), short chitons, Macedonian chlamydes  and boots, and hold sarrissas (long speares or pikes); they are in tears. These two figures constitute the finest examples of Macedonian painting found so far; their style can be readily compared to Florentine mannerism. On the wall two shields are painted. The left shied is decorated with a gorgoneion; the other with the winged thunderbolt, the attribute of Zeus, king of the gods.\n</p><p>Macedonian Tomb \n325 – 300 BC\n</p>\nAgios Athanosios, Thessaloniki, Greece",
          "source": "commons-desc-page"
        },
